Z||000000||camon||10-13-2001||01:34 AM||||I'm going to replace the coil this weekend and i'm looking at the Accel coil listed below. Nothings wrong with the one in it (that i'm aware of...just wanted to put a better coil then the stock one in the fiero) <P>here are the specs:<BR>Accel [Ignition Coil] Super Coil; Ignition Remote Mount Coil; GM HEI Remote Mount Prim Resist 0.3 Ohms Sec Resis 8.8k Ohms; Turn Ratio 134: 1; Max Voltage 48000V;<P>Will this coil give better performance then the stock unit? If so what type of performance increase can be expected (better throttle response ect....)?<P>Eventally I want to goto an MSD or Accel ignition system...but money spites me at this time! <P>I'm also gonna change plugs again (should have bought these to begin with I guess...instead of NGK's) I'm looking at either split fires or Bosche platnium +4's. Which perform better...or is there something else even better? <P>Are there any issues with running any of these listed components in fiero's (coil, plugs)???<P>B.T.W: I have a 87 GT (with stock 2.8liter).<P>Thanks!!!!<P> <BR>||||reg||14
