Z||000005||rogergarrison||10-13-2001||03:13 PM||||whether u get MSD or Accel is just preference. Ive heaard of problems with both. Ive got a Turbo 3.1 (same as 2.8) and Ive had accel bolt in replacement for almost 90K, 4 years with no probs. I did also replace ign module. I have used Bosch Platinum plugs, but decided to give the AC Delcos a try last time.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||camon||10-13-2001||11:36 PM||||Well I bought the accel after all (49.95 at pepboys) and got ACDelco Rapid Fires (3.99 each from Advance Auto Parts). Wanted the MSD but no one local had it, so I settled for the Accel.<P>The plugs were a breeze to put in the second time around (I remembeer how I moaned and complained the first time....and was not looking forward to it this time)...but the old ones (front and rear) went smooth as silk with just a rachet and small extension...couldn't believe it. The coil was a simple install just as I thought it would be. All in all I notice improved throttle response and seems to idle alittle smoother too.<P>The only thing I want to do is check the timing yet (I have the Hayes method but sounds alien). What the heck is this check plug #1 record results then check plug #4 record results...now add the 2 and devide them by 2. Never heard of this type of proceedure...Is it correct????? The timing may be spot on....I just want to check it to be sure!<P>Also the Hayes manual says the timing hash marks (on the crank) are in 2 degree increments (there are 8 hashes). Does this start from front to rear or vise versa. And does it start with "0" or "2".<BR>Example :0 2 4 6 8 10 12 14 (or is it) 2 4 6 8 10 12 14 16 (what is the correct order for the hash marks...and do they run from trunk to firewall or vise versa)??<P>This may be a strange and stupid question but I have never seen this type of procedure or  had it explained in such a incomplete way.||||reg||1
